= Research Interests
The questions the group keeps coming back to

My work combines optimization, network economics and machine learning. The common thread is that
a network is a shared resource, so almost every interesting question is an optimization question
-- and increasingly one that has to be answered from data rather than from a closed-form
solution.

== What we work on

- *Distributed computing and distributed learning.* Splitting a computation across nodes that
  cannot share their raw data, and paying for whatever has to be communicated.
- *Machine learning and deep reinforcement learning for networks.* Learning control policies
  where a model of the system is unavailable or too expensive to keep accurate.
- *Wireless and mobile networking, and the Internet of Things.* Resource allocation in
  interference-limited, energy-limited, and intermittently connected systems.
- *Semantic communication and edge intelligence.* Sending what the receiver needs rather than
  every bit, and putting the inference where the data is.
- *Content caching, adaptive bit-rate streaming, and multipath congestion control.* Where to
  place content and how to deliver it when several paths are available.
- *Network optimization, game theory, and network utility maximization.* The shared toolkit
  behind all of the above.

